.\" This package contributes no subcommand — it claims a file extension. The
.\" page is named mc-mrpack.1 so `mc man mrpack` and the plugin naming rule in
.\" mc-plugins(5) both land here.
.TH MC-MRPACK 1 "" "mc" "mc manual"
.SH NAME
mc-mrpack \- install an mc-managed Minecraft server from a Modrinth modpack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc install
.IB pack .mrpack
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B mc upgrade
.IB pack .mrpack
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mc-mrpack
package teaches
.BR mc (1)
to install from a Modrinth
.B .mrpack
file. It adds no subcommand of its own: it claims the
.B mrpack
extension, so naming such a file where
.B mc install
expects a version routes the work here.
.PP
A
.B .mrpack
pins the Minecraft version, the mod loader and every mod in one artifact, which
is what makes a modded server reproducible. mc reads the pack's index, resolves
the loader, downloads every file, and stages the result; core keeps the lock,
the EULA gate, ownership of
.I /opt/minecraft
and the keys of
.I server.properties
that it owns.
.PP
The loader is detected from the pack's own dependencies. Fabric and NeoForge
packs are supported; a Forge or Quilt pack is refused by name rather than
silently mangled into something that will not boot. A server installed from a
pack can only be upgraded with another pack.
.SH SECURITY
A
.B .mrpack
is attacker-controlled input processed as root, so it is validated in three
phases: everything is parsed and checked with
.I no network access at all,
then files are fetched, then every file is verified.
.IP \(bu 2
Downloads must come from Modrinth's own CDN, over https. A pack that names any
other host is refused.
.IP \(bu 2
Every file must publish a sha512, which is checked after download. A file that
does not match is a failure, not a warning.
.IP \(bu 2
No path in the pack may be written outside the server directory:
.IR .. ,
absolute paths and symlink traversal are all refused before anything is
fetched.
.IP \(bu 2
The pack's own
.I server.properties
is merged, and then mc re-applies the keys it owns \(em so a pack cannot enable
RCON with a password of its choosing, or move the server to a port you did not
pick.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo mc install ~/Downloads/cobblemon\-1.7.0.mrpack \-\-accept\-eula
sudo mc upgrade ~/Downloads/cobblemon\-1.8.0.mrpack
.RE
.fi
.PP
The Java version comes from the pack's Minecraft version and is installed for
you with
.BR \-\-yes .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/minecraft/
Where the staged pack lands, once every file has been verified.
.TP
.I /etc/minecraft/server.mrpack.json
What was installed, so
.B mc upgrade
knows this server came from a pack.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/mc/mc-mrpack
The provider executable. Invoked by mc with a staging directory; see
.BR mc-plugins (5)
for the protocol.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc (1),
.BR mc-config (5),
.BR mc-plugins (5),
.BR mc-backup (1)
